   "qtype": "numeric",
   "section": "Section B",
   "stem": "A curve $e^{y}\\sin x\\,dy + \\cos x(e^{y} + 1)dx = 0$ passes through $\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{2}, 0\\right)$. then find $e^{y\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{6}\\right)}$.",
