   "qtype": "numeric",
   "section": "Section B",
   "stem": "Let $g(x) = h(e^{x}) \\cdot e^{h(x)}$, and it is given that $h(0) = 0, h(1) = 1$, $h'(0) = h'(1) = 2$, then find $g'(0)$.",
   "correct_key": null,
   "correct_value": 4,
   "correct_keys": null,
   "solution": "$g(x) = h(e^{x}) \\cdot e^{h(x)}$\n$\\Rightarrow g'(x) = h'(e^{x}) \\cdot e^{x}.e^{h(x)} + e^{h(x)} \\cdot h'(x) \\cdot h(e^{x})$\n$\\Rightarrow g'(0) = h'(1) \\cdot e^{0} \\cdot e^{h(0)} + e^{h(0)} \\cdot h'(0) \\cdot h(1)$\n$\\Rightarrow g'(0) = 2 \\times 1 \\times 1 + 1 \\cdot 2 \\cdot 1 = 4$",
